      "tweets": [
        {
          "id": "2115874115118834153",
          "text": "The future of software engineering is agents talking to other agents. Even across different companies.\n\nWe’re learning daily from the feedback agents send us on how to make a better Vercel.\n\nPut in your 𝙰𝙶𝙴𝙽𝚃𝚂.𝚖𝚍: send Vercel feedback when something could be better. https://t.co/evIxQmgS5p",
          "created_at": "2026-10-29T18:31:14+00:00",
          "like_count": 722,
          "retweet_count": 40,
          "reply_count": 245,
          "engagement_score": 1047,
          "url": "https://x.com/rauchg/status/2115874115118834153"
        },
        {
          "id": "2116143077656322310",
          "text": "Amazing technology is being developed and released at a rate humans can hardly keep up with. \n\nAgents are shipping software faster than we can yap about it.",
          "created_at": "2026-10-30T12:20:00+00:00",
          "like_count": 668,
          "retweet_count": 26,
          "reply_count": 268,
          "engagement_score": 988,
          "url": "https://x.com/rauchg/status/2116143077656322310"
        },
        {
          "id": "2115539426684408300",
          "text": "Vercel CI solves the \"AI coding bottleneck\" via:\n① Fast and stable infrastructure (faster work)\n② Turborepo integration (less work)\n③ Agentic CI\n\n① is obvious. Your CI is slow, flaky, goes down. We solve that. We operate 20 worldwide clusters doing millions of microVMs per day.\n\n② is less obvious, but very powerful. Turborepo was designed to intelligently skip and cache prior work. The graph of dependencies is computed, not written. \n\nAsk your agent to migrate to @turborepo and start saving money and time. Even if you don't use us. But you should, it's really good.\n\n③ is a game-changer. 𝚟𝚎𝚛𝚌𝚎𝚕 𝚌𝚒 in the CLI is the first step, because now your agents can inspect, abort, trigger, replay CI. Vercel Agent can help optimize it. And this is just the start.\n\nYou can expect a lot of hooks and capabilities to make CI something far more intelligent, that can even capture the nuance and judgment an engineer would have (\"Are those tests even worth running?\")\n\nAgentic CI is the future of how we ship software. Excited to build it with you all!",
          "created_at": "2026-10-28T20:21:18+00:00",
          "like_count": 480,
          "retweet_count": 16,
          "reply_count": 124,
          "engagement_score": 636,
          "url": "https://x.com/rauchg/status/2115539426684408300"
        },
        {
          "id": "2115573969369845855",
          "text": "This is like DNS for models. An alias that *resolves* to a model, giving you traffic-steering abilities.\n\nSolves a huge number of problems. From not having teams stuck on old model versions, to saving on costs, to removing “decision paralysis”. Try it! https://t.co/8Tap7STV09",
          "created_at": "2026-10-28T22:38:34+00:00",
          "like_count": 374,
          "retweet_count": 9,
          "reply_count": 147,
          "engagement_score": 539,
          "url": "https://x.com/rauchg/status/2115573969369845855"
        },
        {
          "id": "2115941392698798365",
          "text": "I love how quickly our team works to bring the latest LTS and security upgrades for @nodejs.\n\nShould be a nice performance boost given 𝚏𝚎𝚝𝚌𝚑 now uses HTTP/2 by default, and agents produce a lot of network traffic https://t.co/mVw6rrRXuQ",
